(--- the manifest ---

 Things. 'gen thing field first' and 'gen thing field count' bracket
 this thing's run in the field lists; the method pair does the same.)

a list called gen_thing_names is [].
(Both written forms, computed once when the name is drawn rather than
 on every emit. A phrase and its two renderings are not the same string
 and every one of them is part of what this program's prelude IS, so the
 manifest holds all three and the accessors below are plain reads.

 Not a speed fix, and measured rather than assumed: it made no
 difference to tests/200_never_emitted's 2000-program sweep. What DID
 get slower is inherent - `'the survey marker's 'the north offset'` is
 four times the bytes of `i1's x1`, every generated program is
 correspondingly bigger, and the layout pass walks every byte. The sweep
 went from 2m12 on main to about 3m40 here, which is why test.sh's
 per-test cap moved.)
a list called gen_thing_written_names is [].
a list called gen_thing_possessives is [].
a list called gen_thing_field_first is [].
a list called gen_thing_field_count is [].
a list called gen_thing_method_first is [].
a list called gen_thing_method_count is [].

(Fields. `kind`: 0 number, 1 float, 2 boolean, 3 time, 4 a nested thing
 - the five LANGUAGE.md:985-987 allows, and `target` names the nested
 thing for kind 4.)

a list called gen_field_names is [].
a list called gen_field_written_names is [].
a list called gen_field_possessives is [].
a list called gen_field_owner is [].
a list called gen_field_kind is [].
a list called gen_field_target is [].

(Methods. `kind`: 0 a maker - first parameter is a number, so only the
 type possessive reaches it (LANGUAGE.md:1590); 1 a receiver - first
 parameter is the owner, so both call forms reach it
 (LANGUAGE.md:1611).)

a list called gen_method_names is [].
a list called gen_method_written_names is [].
a list called gen_method_owner is [].
a list called gen_method_kind is [].

(A method's own parameter and the local it returns. Both are drawn from
 the parameter pool at build time rather than at emit time, so the
 manifest is the single record of what this program's prelude says and
 the emitter only reads it.)

a list called gen_method_param_written is [].
a list called gen_method_param_possessives is [].
a list called gen_method_local_written is [].
a list called gen_method_local_possessives is [].

(Which of the owner's number fields this method writes, or 0 when the
 owner has none - a thing whose only fields are floats, booleans, times
 or nested things still gets a method, it just returns a fresh instance
 without writing anything. The leaf that calls the method reads this
 field back, so it prints what the call put there rather than a default
 that happened to be nearby.)

a list called gen_method_field is [].

(Functions. `returns` is 1 when the body ends in `Return a number,` and
 0 when it only prints - a call site has to know, because `Print <call>`
 needs a value and a bare call does not.)

a list called gen_function_names is [].
a list called gen_function_written_names is [].
a list called gen_function_arity is [].
a list called gen_function_first_param is [].
a list called gen_function_returns is [].

(The local a returning function computes into, so `Return a number, r`
 stops being the same line in every program.)

a list called gen_function_local_written is [].

(Parameters. `kind`: 0 number, 1 text.)

a list called gen_param_names is [].
a list called gen_param_written_names is [].
a list called gen_param_kind is [].

(Flags. `kind`: 0 text, 1 number, 2 boolean - the three
 LANGUAGE.md:4737-4745 lists. `default` is the literal as it is written
 after `with default`, or "" for a flag that has none. `role` is 1 for
 the one flag that carries the scratch directory and 0 for every other.)

a list called gen_flag_names is [].
a list called gen_flag_written_names is [].
a list called gen_flag_short is [].
a list called gen_flag_long is [].
a list called gen_flag_kind is [].
a list called gen_flag_default is [].
a list called gen_flag_role is [].

(The scratch flag, as the rest of the fuzzer needs it: the name a
 generated program writes to read it, and the alias loop_gen.vox passes
 on the command line. Both are "" when this program declares no scratch
 flag, which is every program that did not choose file I/O.)

a text called gen_scratch_flag is "".

a text called gen_scratch_argv is "".

(The two prelude functions that are not ordinary manifest functions
 because something else decides whether they exist: the flag reader
 (gen_uses_flag_reader) and the grid sink (gen_uses_grid, and its arity
 is gen_grid_depth). Their names are drawn from the same function pool
 and spent from the same cycle, so they cannot collide with an ordinary
 function.)

a text called gen_reader_name is "".

a text called gen_grid_sink_name is "".

a list called gen_grid_sink_params is [].

a text called gen_grid_sink_local is "".

(--- query results ---

 A query returns a boolean and leaves what it found in these, which is
 the cross-call scratch pattern harness.vox uses for 'the last status'
 and scripts/invariants.vox for 'the slot values'. Vox returns one
 value, and a thing plus a field plus an inner field is three.)

a number called gen_pick_thing is 0.

a number called gen_pick_field is 0.

a number called gen_pick_inner_thing is 0.

a number called gen_pick_inner_field is 0.

a number called gen_pick_maker is 0.

a number called gen_pick_receiver is 0.

a number called gen_pick_function is 0.

a number called gen_pick_flag is 0.

(--- small helpers ---)

(A stride for a vocabulary of prime length: anything from 1 to len-1 is
 coprime with a prime, so the walk visits every word.)

To 'gen stride for' with a number called 'how many words'.
    a number called 'the room' is 'how many words' minus 1.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'the room'.
    Return a number, 'the draw' add 1.

(A long alias from a phrase: spaces become hyphens behind a `--`. Two
 flags in one program have distinct phrases, so their aliases are
 distinct too. Hand-verified that `--the-caption` parses and matches.

 The three buffers below are program level and 'clear'ed per call
 (Defect 17): declared locally, each is one more 4 KB allocation per
 call never freed until program exit.)

a buffer called 'the dashed alias source view' is "".

a buffer called 'the dashed alias bytes' is "--".

a buffer called 'one dashed alias byte' is " ".

To 'gen dashed alias' with a text called phrase.
    clear 'the dashed alias source view'.
    append phrase to 'the dashed alias source view'.
    clear 'the dashed alias bytes'.
    append "--" to 'the dashed alias bytes'.
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the dashed alias source view's size.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the byte here' is byte 'the position' of 'the dashed alias source view',
        a number called 'the written byte' is 'the byte here',
        If 'the byte here' is 32 then,
            Set 'the written byte' to 45.
        Set byte 1 of 'one dashed alias byte' to 'the written byte',
        append 'one dashed alias byte' to 'the dashed alias bytes',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Return a text, 'the dashed alias bytes' as text.

(One unspent letter, as a short alias. The walk takes a coprime stride
 over the alphabet so no two flags in a program share a letter and the
 letters a program uses are not consecutive.)

To 'gen short alias'.
    Set gen_letter_spent to gen_letter_spent add 1.
    a number called 'the step' is gen_letter_spent multiply gen_letter_stride.
    a number called 'the raw slot' is 'the step' add gen_letter_offset.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the raw slot' modulo 26.
    a number called 'the position' is 'the slot' add 1.
    a text called 'the letter' is element 'the position' of gen_alias_letters.
    a text called 'the alias' is "-{'the letter'}".
    Return a text, 'the alias'.

(--- reading the manifest back out ---

 A name is stored as a bare phrase and written in one of two forms.
 These are the only places the generator turns a manifest row into
 source text, so a name that needs quoting cannot be written unquoted by
 accident.)

To 'gen thing written' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_written_names.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen thing possessive' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_possessives.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen field written' with a number called 'the field'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the field' of gen_field_written_names.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen field possessive' with a number called 'the field'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the field' of gen_field_possessives.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen method written' with a number called 'the method'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the method' of gen_method_written_names.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen function written' with a number called 'the function'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the function' of gen_function_written_names.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen parameter written' with a number called 'the parameter'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the parameter' of gen_param_written_names.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen method param written' with a number called 'the method'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the method' of gen_method_param_written.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen method param possessive' with a number called 'the method'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the method' of gen_method_param_possessives.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen method local written' with a number called 'the method'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the method' of gen_method_local_written.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen method local possessive' with a number called 'the method'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the method' of gen_method_local_possessives.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen function local written' with a number called 'the function'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the function' of gen_function_local_written.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

To 'gen flag written' with a number called 'the flag'.
    a text called 'the name' is element 'the flag' of gen_flag_written_names.
    Return a text, 'the name'.

(The type keyword for a field, as it is written in a definition.)

To 'gen field type written' with a number called 'the field'.
    a number called 'the kind' is element 'the field' of gen_field_kind.
    If 'the kind' is 0 then,
        Return a text, "number".
    If 'the kind' is 1 then,
        Return a text, "float".
    If 'the kind' is 2 then,
        Return a text, "boolean".
    If 'the kind' is 3 then,
        Return a text, "time".
    a number called 'the target' is element 'the field' of gen_field_target.
    a text called 'the target name' is 'gen thing written' of 'the target'.
    Return a text, 'the target name'.

(A field's default, written after `is`, or "" for a field that takes its
 type's zero value. LANGUAGE.md:960 says a field without a default takes
 its type's zero value, so BOTH forms are legal and which one a field
 gets is drawn. A nested thing has no literal to default to and a time
 has none either, so those two never carry one.)

To 'gen field default written' with a number called 'the field'.
    a number called 'the kind' is element 'the field' of gen_field_kind.
    If 'the kind' is 3 then,
        Return a text, "".
    If 'the kind' is 4 then,
        Return a text, "".
    a number called 'the default draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    If 'the default draw' is less than 6 then,
        Return a text, "".
    If 'the kind' is 0 then,
        a text called 'a number literal' is 'literal integer',
        Return a text, 'a number literal'.
    If 'the kind' is 1 then,
        a text called 'a float literal' is 'gen extreme float',
        Return a text, 'a float literal'.
    a number called 'the truth draw' is 'rng below' of 11.
    If 'the truth draw' is less than 6 then,
        Return a text, "false".
    Return a text, "true".

