    Set gen_grid_sink_name to "".
    Set gen_grid_sink_local to "".
    'gen reset manifest cycles'.
    'gen build manifest things'.
    'gen build manifest functions'.
    'gen build manifest flags'.
    'gen build manifest extras'.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen reset manifest cycles'.
    Set gen_type_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many types' is gen_type_words's length.
    Set gen_type_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many types'.
    Set gen_type_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many types'.
    Set gen_field_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many fields' is gen_field_words's length.
    Set gen_field_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many fields'.
    Set gen_field_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many fields'.
    Set gen_maker_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many makers' is gen_maker_words's length.
    Set gen_maker_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many makers'.
    Set gen_maker_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many makers'.
    Set gen_receiver_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many receivers' is gen_receiver_words's length.
    Set gen_receiver_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many receivers'.
    Set gen_receiver_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many receivers'.
    Set gen_function_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many functions' is gen_function_words's length.
    Set gen_function_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many functions'.
    Set gen_function_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many functions'.
    Set gen_param_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many parameters' is gen_parameter_words's length.
    Set gen_param_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many parameters'.
    Set gen_param_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many parameters'.
    Set gen_flagname_spent to 0.
    a number called 'how many flag words' is gen_flag_words's length.
    Set gen_flagname_offset to 'rng below' of 'how many flag words'.
    Set gen_flagname_stride to 'gen stride for' of 'how many flag words'.
    Set gen_letter_spent to 0.
    Set gen_letter_offset to 'rng below' of 26.
    a number called 'how many strides' is gen_alias_strides's length.
    a number called 'the stride draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many strides'.
    a number called 'the stride slot' is 'the stride draw' add 1.
    Set gen_letter_stride to element 'the stride slot' of gen_alias_strides.
    Return a number, 0.

(How many things. Zero is a real possibility: LANGUAGE.md nowhere says a
 program has any things, and a program with none is legal Vox. Every
 leaf that wants one asks the manifest first.)

To 'gen build manifest things'.
    a number called 'how many things' is 'rng below' of 7.
    a number called 'the thing made' is 0.
    While 'the thing made' is less than 'how many things',
        'gen build one thing',
        Set 'the thing made' to 'the thing made' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen build one thing'.
    Set gen_type_spent to gen_type_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the type phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_type_words and gen_type_spent and gen_type_offset and gen_type_stride.
    append 'the type phrase' to gen_thing_names.
    a text called 'the type written' is 'gen written name' of 'the type phrase'.
    append 'the type written' to gen_thing_written_names.
    a text called 'the type possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the type phrase'.
    append 'the type possessive' to gen_thing_possessives.
    a number called 'this thing' is gen_thing_names's length.
    (A thing needs at least one field - hand-verified against 0.4.7:
     `A thing called sighting has.` is rejected with "A thing needs at
     least one field". That floor is the only thing pinned; no rule
     anywhere sets a ceiling, so the count above it is drawn.)
    a number called 'the field start' is gen_field_names's length add 1.
    a number called 'the field draw' is 'rng below' of 4.
    a number called 'how many fields' is 'the field draw' add 1.
    a number called 'the field made' is 0.
    While 'the field made' is less than 'how many fields',
        'gen build one field' of 'this thing',
        Set 'the field made' to 'the field made' add 1.
    append 'the field start' to gen_thing_field_first.
    append 'how many fields' to gen_thing_field_count.
    a number called 'the method start' is gen_method_names's length add 1.
    (Weighted toward two, for the reason 'gen field kind draw' gives: a
     thing with a maker AND a receiver is the one shape the member leaf
     can drive, and a flat draw over 0/1/2 left it reachable in 4% of
     programs. Zero methods stays common - most things have none.)
    a number called 'the method draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    a number called 'how many methods' is 2.
    If 'the method draw' is less than 3 then,
        Set 'how many methods' to 0.
    If 'the method draw' is greater than 2 and 'the method draw' is less than 7 then,
        Set 'how many methods' to 1.
    'gen build methods for' of 'this thing' and 'how many methods'.
    append 'the method start' to gen_thing_method_first.
    append 'how many methods' to gen_thing_method_count.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen build one field' with a number called 'this thing'.
    Set gen_field_spent to gen_field_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the field phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_field_words and gen_field_spent and gen_field_offset and gen_field_stride.
    append 'the field phrase' to gen_field_names.
    a text called 'the field written' is 'gen written name' of 'the field phrase'.
    append 'the field written' to gen_field_written_names.
    a text called 'the field possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the field phrase'.
    append 'the field possessive' to gen_field_possessives.
    append 'this thing' to gen_field_owner.
    (LANGUAGE.md:985-987: a field may be number, float, boolean, time,
     or any PREVIOUSLY DEFINED thing. text, list, map and buffer are
     deferred, so these five are the whole space and the draw covers it.
     The nesting kind falls back to a number when there is no earlier
     thing to nest, which is the "previously defined" half of the rule.)
    a number called 'the earlier things' is 'this thing' minus 1.
    a number called 'the kind' is 'gen field kind draw'.
    If 'the kind' is 4 and 'the earlier things' is 0 then,
        Set 'the kind' to 0.
    append 'the kind' to gen_field_kind.
    a number called 'the target' is 0.
    If 'the kind' is 4 then,
        a number called 'the target draw' is 'rng below' of 'the earlier things',
        Set 'the target' to 'the target draw' add 1.
    append 'the target' to gen_field_target.
    Return a number, 0.

(All five kinds, weighted rather than uniform. A NUMBER field is the
 only one the statement stream can write a literal into, so a thing
 whose fields are all floats and booleans is a thing no leaf can use -
 and with a flat draw over five kinds, 57% of things came out that way
 and the member leaf's reach fell from 27 programs in 150 to 6.

 Weighting a draw is not the sameness CLAUDE.md forbids: no line of
 LANGUAGE.md says how many fields of which type a thing has, so every
 distribution over the five is equally legal and none of them is a
 repeatable PATTERN. What would be a defect is a fixed count or a fixed
 type, and neither is here - every kind stays reachable, floats,
 booleans, times and nested things included.)

To 'gen field kind draw'.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    If 'the draw' is less than 6 then,
        Return a number, 0.
    If 'the draw' is less than 8 then,
        Return a number, 1.
    If 'the draw' is less than 10 then,
        Return a number, 2.
    If 'the draw' is less than 11 then,
        Return a number, 3.
    Return a number, 4.

(Two methods means one of each kind, because a thing that has both is
 the one shape 'gen leaf thing member' needs - the maker brings an
 instance into being through the type possessive and the receiver
 transforms it through the instance possessive. Which of the two is
 declared first is drawn; nothing pins it.

 Prime moduli throughout. This LCG's low bits are correlated - the
 hazard is documented above 'gen leaf loop control' and has caught this
 generator out three times - and a plain `'rng below' of 2` here would
 lock the kind of a single method to the parity of the draw before it.)

To 'gen build methods for' with a number called 'this thing' and a number called 'how many methods'.
    If 'how many methods' is 0 then,
        Return a number, 0.
    If 'how many methods' is 1 then,
        a number called 'the kind draw' is 'rng below' of 13,
        a number called 'the only kind' is 0,
        If 'the kind draw' is greater than 6 then,
            Set 'the only kind' to 1.
        'gen build one method' of 'this thing' and 'the only kind',
        Return a number, 0.
    a number called 'the order draw' is 'rng below' of 11.
    If 'the order draw' is less than 6 then,
        'gen build one method' of 'this thing' and 0,
        'gen build one method' of 'this thing' and 1,
        Return a number, 0.
    'gen build one method' of 'this thing' and 1.
    'gen build one method' of 'this thing' and 0.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen build one method' with a number called 'this thing' and a number called 'the kind'.
    a text called 'the method phrase' is "".
    If 'the kind' is 0 then,
        Set gen_maker_spent to gen_maker_spent add 1,
        Set 'the method phrase' to 'gen cycled word' of gen_maker_words and gen_maker_spent and gen_maker_offset and gen_maker_stride.
    If 'the kind' is 1 then,
        Set gen_receiver_spent to gen_receiver_spent add 1,
        Set 'the method phrase' to 'gen cycled word' of gen_receiver_words and gen_receiver_spent and gen_receiver_offset and gen_receiver_stride.
    append 'the method phrase' to gen_method_names.
    a text called 'the method written' is 'gen written name' of 'the method phrase'.
    append 'the method written' to gen_method_written_names.
    append 'this thing' to gen_method_owner.
    append 'the kind' to gen_method_kind.
    a text called 'the parameter phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the parameter written' is 'gen written name' of 'the parameter phrase'.
    append 'the parameter written' to gen_method_param_written.
    a text called 'the parameter possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the parameter phrase'.
    append 'the parameter possessive' to gen_method_param_possessives.
    a text called 'the local phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the local written' is 'gen written name' of 'the local phrase'.
    append 'the local written' to gen_method_local_written.
    a text called 'the local possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the local phrase'.
    append 'the local possessive' to gen_method_local_possessives.
    a number called 'the written field' is 'gen a number field of' of 'this thing'.
    append 'the written field' to gen_method_field.
    Return a number, 0.

(One unspent parameter phrase. A method's parameter, a method's local
 and an ordinary function's parameters all come from here, so no two
 names inside one function body can collide however the draws fall.)

To 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    Set gen_param_spent to gen_param_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_parameter_words and gen_param_spent and gen_param_offset and gen_param_stride.
    Return a text, 'the phrase'.

(How many functions, and of what shape. LANGUAGE.md:796-802 puts no
 ceiling on either count or arity, and says parameters are optional - so
 zero functions and zero-parameter functions are both ordinary, and the
 old prelude's "exactly four, arities 0/1/2/1" was ours alone.)

To 'gen build manifest functions'.
    a number called 'how many functions' is 'rng below' of 7.
    a number called 'the function made' is 0.
    While 'the function made' is less than 'how many functions',
        'gen build one function',
        Set 'the function made' to 'the function made' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen build one function'.
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the function phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    append 'the function phrase' to gen_function_names.
    a text called 'the function written' is 'gen written name' of 'the function phrase'.
    append 'the function written' to gen_function_written_names.
    a number called 'the parameter start' is gen_param_names's length add 1.
    (Arity 0 to 3, weighted a little toward two. A grid clause fills one
     parameter each and the leaf that chains two of them therefore needs
     a two-number callee; under a flat draw that leaf's reach fell from
     37 programs in 150 to 14. Every arity stays reachable, three
     included - which the old fixed prelude's 0/1/2 never was.)
    a number called 'the arity draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    a number called 'how many parameters' is 0.
    If 'the arity draw' is greater than 2 and 'the arity draw' is less than 6 then,
        Set 'how many parameters' to 1.
    If 'the arity draw' is greater than 5 and 'the arity draw' is less than 10 then,
        Set 'how many parameters' to 2.
    If 'the arity draw' is greater than 9 then,
        Set 'how many parameters' to 3.
    a number called 'the parameter made' is 0.
    While 'the parameter made' is less than 'how many parameters',
        a text called 'the parameter phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase',
        append 'the parameter phrase' to gen_param_names,
        a text called 'the parameter written' is 'gen written name' of 'the parameter phrase',
        append 'the parameter written' to gen_param_written_names,
        a number called 'the type draw' is 'rng below' of 13,
        a number called 'the parameter kind' is 0,
        If 'the type draw' is greater than 9 then,
            Set 'the parameter kind' to 1.
        append 'the parameter kind' to gen_param_kind,
        Set 'the parameter made' to 'the parameter made' add 1.
    append 'the parameter start' to gen_function_first_param.
    append 'how many parameters' to gen_function_arity.
    (A function that returns and one that only prints are both ordinary
     Vox (LANGUAGE.md:733-741 shows both), so which this is gets drawn.
     A call site reads it back rather than assuming: `Print <call>` needs
     a value and a bare call does not.)
    a number called 'the return draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    a number called 'the returns' is 1.
    If 'the return draw' is less than 4 then,
        Set 'the returns' to 0.
    append 'the returns' to gen_function_returns.
    a text called 'the local phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the local written' is 'gen written name' of 'the local phrase'.
    append 'the local written' to gen_function_local_written.
    Return a number, 0.

(How many flags, and where the scratch flag sits among them. The scratch
 flag is declared only when this program chose file I/O, because that is
 the only reason it exists; loop_gen.vox passes its alias only when it
 was declared, so a program with no flags is invoked with no flags.
 Verified against 0.4.7 that an undeclared flag on argv is neither a
 compile nor a runtime error - it falls through to `arguments's all` -
 so passing one anyway would have been harmless, but there is no reason
 to.

 Its SLOT is drawn rather than fixed at the end: nothing pins the order
 of flag declarations, and a scratch flag always written last would be
 exactly the kind of sameness with no citation this work is removing.)

To 'gen build manifest flags'.
    a number called 'how many ordinary flags' is 'rng below' of 5.
    a number called 'how many slots' is 'how many ordinary flags'.
    a number called 'the scratch slot' is 0.
    If gen_does_file_io then,
        Set 'how many slots' to 'how many ordinary flags' add 1,
        a number called 'the slot draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many slots',
        Set 'the scratch slot' to 'the slot draw' add 1.
    a number called 'the flag made' is 0.
    While 'the flag made' is less than 'how many slots',
        a number called 'this slot' is 'the flag made' add 1,
        a number called 'the role' is 0,
        If 'this slot' is 'the scratch slot' then,
            Set 'the role' to 1.
        'gen build one flag' of 'the role',
        Set 'the flag made' to 'the flag made' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen build one flag' with a number called 'the role'.
    Set gen_flagname_spent to gen_flagname_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the flag phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_flag_words and gen_flagname_spent and gen_flagname_offset and gen_flagname_stride.
    append 'the flag phrase' to gen_flag_names.
    a text called 'the flag written' is 'gen written name' of 'the flag phrase'.
    append 'the flag written' to gen_flag_written_names.
    (Both aliases, always. Hand-verified against 0.4.7 that a schema
     with only a long alias is rejected - "Expected long flag alias
     string like '--number'" - so the `"-x" or "--long"` shape is the
     language's rule, not ours, and it is the one piece of the flag line
     that is the same in every program by right.)
    a text called 'the short alias' is 'gen short alias'.
    append 'the short alias' to gen_flag_short.
    a text called 'the long alias' is 'gen dashed alias' of 'the flag phrase'.
    append 'the long alias' to gen_flag_long.
    (The scratch flag carries a path, so it is a text. Every other flag
     draws across the three types LANGUAGE.md:4737-4745 lists.)
    a number called 'the kind' is 0.
    If 'the role' is 0 then,
        Set 'the kind' to 'rng below' of 3.
    append 'the kind' to gen_flag_kind.
    a text called 'the default' is 'gen flag default for' of 'the kind'.
    append 'the default' to gen_flag_default.
    append 'the role' to gen_flag_role.
    If 'the role' is 1 then,
        Set gen_scratch_flag to 'the flag written',
        (Either alias reaches the same flag, so which one the harness
         passes is drawn too - the short and long paths through the
         parser are different code.)
        Set gen_scratch_argv to 'the long alias',
        a number called 'the alias draw' is 'rng below' of 11,
        If 'the alias draw' is less than 5 then,
            Set gen_scratch_argv to 'the short alias'.
    Return a number, 0.

(A default, or none. LANGUAGE.md:4762-4763: a flag with no default holds
 its type's empty value, so both forms are legal for every type and
 which one a flag gets is drawn. Hand-verified against 0.4.7 that a
 boolean flag takes `with default true` and a number flag takes a
 fifteen-digit default, both of which the old prelude never wrote.

 `and is required` is the one modifier never drawn: a required flag that
 this program's argv does not supply aborts at runtime, and the
 invariant every generated program must hold is that it compiles AND
 runs.)

To 'gen flag default for' with a number called 'the kind'.
    a number called 'the default draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    If 'the default draw' is less than 7 then,
        Return a text, "".
    If 'the kind' is 0 then,
        a text called 'a word' is 'gen word from' of gen_type_words,
        Return a text, "\"{'a word'}\"".
    If 'the kind' is 1 then,
        a number called 'the digit count' is 'rng below' of 15 add 1,
        a text called 'the digits' is 'gen random digits' of 'the digit count',
        Return a text, 'the digits'.
    a number called 'the truth draw' is 'rng below' of 11.
    If 'the truth draw' is less than 5 then,
        Return a text, "false".
    Return a text, "true".

(The two prelude functions whose existence something else decides. Their
 names come out of the ordinary function cycle so they cannot collide
 with a manifest function, and they are drawn whether or not the program
 uses them - drawing them conditionally would make the seed-to-name
 mapping depend on a decision taken elsewhere, which is exactly the bug
 the 'gen reset value names' comment in 'gen program' records.)

To 'gen build manifest extras'.
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the reader phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    Set gen_reader_name to 'gen written name' of 'the reader phrase'.
    Set gen_function_spent to gen_function_spent add 1.
    a text called 'the sink phrase' is 'gen cycled word' of gen_function_words and gen_function_spent and gen_function_offset and gen_function_stride.
    Set gen_grid_sink_name to 'gen written name' of 'the sink phrase'.
    (The sink's parameters are named from the parameter cycle like any
     other function's, so `p1..pN` is gone from the corpus too. Drawn to
     the depth this program committed to in 'gen program'.)
    a number called 'the parameter made' is 0.
    While 'the parameter made' is less than gen_grid_depth,
        a text called 'the parameter phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase',
        a text called 'the parameter name' is 'gen written name' of 'the parameter phrase',
        append 'the parameter name' to gen_grid_sink_params,
        Set 'the parameter made' to 'the parameter made' add 1.
    a text called 'the local phrase' is 'gen fresh parameter phrase'.
    Set gen_grid_sink_local to 'gen written name' of 'the local phrase'.
    Return a number, 0.

(--- queries ---

 Each answers "does this program's prelude have the shape I need", and
 leaves what it found in the gen_pick_* globals. A leaf that gets false
 is not eligible and stands aside for one that always works.)

(A thing with at least one number field: what every leaf that writes a
 field needs, since a number is the only field type the statement stream
 has a literal for.)

To 'gen manifest pick a plain thing'.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'how many fields' is gen_field_names's length.
    a number called 'the field' is 1.
    While 'the field' is less than or equal to 'how many fields',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the field' of gen_field_kind,
        If 'the kind' is 0 then,
            append 'the field' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the field' to 'the field' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_field to element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    Set gen_pick_thing to element gen_pick_field of gen_field_owner.
    Return a boolean, true.

(A thing holding a thing that has a number field: the chained possessive
 shape. The old prelude guaranteed it with t3; nothing in the language
 does, so a program without one simply cannot host this leaf.)

To 'gen manifest pick a nested thing'.
    Set gen_nested_outer to [].
    Set gen_nested_inner to [].
    a number called 'how many fields' is gen_field_names's length.
    a number called 'the field' is 1.
    While 'the field' is less than or equal to 'how many fields',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the field' of gen_field_kind,
        If 'the kind' is 4 then,
            'gen collect a number field of' of 'the field'.
        Set 'the field' to 'the field' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is gen_nested_outer's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_field to element 'the slot' of gen_nested_outer.
    Set gen_pick_inner_field to element 'the slot' of gen_nested_inner.
    Set gen_pick_thing to element gen_pick_field of gen_field_owner.
    Set gen_pick_inner_thing to element gen_pick_field of gen_field_target.
    Return a boolean, true.

(A thing with a maker AND a receiver, plus a number field for both to
 write - the shape 'gen leaf thing member' drives. All three have to
 land on the same thing, so the search is per thing rather than per
 member.)

To 'gen manifest pick a thing with both members'.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'how many things' is gen_thing_names's length.
    a number called 'the thing' is 1.
    While 'the thing' is less than or equal to 'how many things',
        a boolean called 'this one fits' is 'gen thing has both members' of 'the thing',
        If 'this one fits' then,
            append 'the thing' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the thing' to 'the thing' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_thing to element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    'gen locate members of' of gen_pick_thing.
    'gen locate a number field of' of gen_pick_thing.
    Return a boolean, true.

To 'gen thing has both members' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a number called 'the first method' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_first.
    a number called 'how many methods' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_count.
    a boolean called 'a maker is here' is false.
    a boolean called 'a receiver is here' is false.
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    While 'the step' is less than 'how many methods',
        a number called 'the method' is 'the first method' add 'the step',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the method' of gen_method_kind,
        If 'the kind' is 0 then,
            Set 'a maker is here' to true.
        If 'the kind' is 1 then,
            Set 'a receiver is here' to true.
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    If 'a maker is here' is false then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If 'a receiver is here' is false then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a boolean called 'a number field is here' is 'gen thing has a number field' of 'the thing'.
    Return a boolean, 'a number field is here'.

To 'gen thing has a number field' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a number called 'the field' is 'gen a number field of' of 'the thing'.
    If 'the field' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Return a boolean, true.

(One of this thing's number fields, drawn, or 0 when it has none. The
 only search that walks a single owner's run, so everything that needs a
 writable field goes through it.)

To 'gen a number field of' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a number called 'the first field' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_field_first.
    a number called 'how many fields' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_field_count.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    While 'the step' is less than 'how many fields',
        a number called 'the field' is 'the first field' add 'the step',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the field' of gen_field_kind,
        If 'the kind' is 0 then,
            append 'the field' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a number, 0.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    a number called 'the chosen' is element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    Return a number, 'the chosen'.

(Side effects, both of them: 'gen locate members of' fills
 gen_pick_maker and gen_pick_receiver, 'gen locate a number field of'
 fills gen_pick_field. Only ever called for a thing already known to
 have what is being looked for.)

To 'gen locate members of' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a number called 'the first method' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_first.
    a number called 'how many methods' is element 'the thing' of gen_thing_method_count.
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    While 'the step' is less than 'how many methods',
        a number called 'the method' is 'the first method' add 'the step',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the method' of gen_method_kind,
        If 'the kind' is 0 then,
            Set gen_pick_maker to 'the method'.
        If 'the kind' is 1 then,
            Set gen_pick_receiver to 'the method'.
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

To 'gen locate a number field of' with a number called 'the thing'.
    a number called 'the field' is 'gen a number field of' of 'the thing'.
    Set gen_pick_field to 'the field'.
    Return a number, 0.

(The nested search's two accumulators. A pair of parallel lists rather
 than a returned tuple, for the reason the header gives: Vox returns one
 value and this search finds two.)

a list called gen_nested_outer is [].

a list called gen_nested_inner is [].

To 'gen collect a number field of' with a number called 'the outer field'.
    a number called 'the target' is element 'the outer field' of gen_field_target.
    a number called 'the first field' is element 'the target' of gen_thing_field_first.
    a number called 'how many fields' is element 'the target' of gen_thing_field_count.
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    While 'the step' is less than 'how many fields',
        a number called 'the field' is 'the first field' add 'the step',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the field' of gen_field_kind,
        If 'the kind' is 0 then,
            append 'the outer field' to gen_nested_outer,
            append 'the field' to gen_nested_inner.
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    Return a number, 0.

(Any function at all. The call leaves read its arity and parameter types
 back and write a call that matches, so every shape the manifest can
 hold is callable - including the three-parameter shape the old
 hardcoded f1/f2/f3 could never reach.)

To 'gen manifest pick a function'.
    a number called 'how many functions' is gen_function_names's length.
    If 'how many functions' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many functions'.
    Set gen_pick_function to 'the draw' add 1.
    Return a boolean, true.

(A function that yields a value, for a call site that prints the result.)

To 'gen manifest pick a returning function'.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'how many functions' is gen_function_names's length.
    a number called 'the function' is 1.
    While 'the function' is less than or equal to 'how many functions',
        a number called 'the returns' is element 'the function' of gen_function_returns,
        If 'the returns' is 1 then,
            append 'the function' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the function' to 'the function' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_function to element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    Return a boolean, true.

(A function whose parameters are all numbers and of which there are at
 least this many: what a grid clause needs, since `each ... from ... to
 ...` yields numbers and fills one parameter each. The caller reads the
 arity back and writes that many clauses.)

To 'gen manifest pick a numeric function from' with a number called 'the least arity'.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'how many functions' is gen_function_names's length.
    a number called 'the function' is 1.
    While 'the function' is less than or equal to 'how many functions',
        a boolean called 'this one fits' is 'gen function is all numbers from' of 'the function' and 'the least arity',
        If 'this one fits' then,
            append 'the function' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the function' to 'the function' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_function to element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    Return a boolean, true.

To 'gen function is all numbers from' with a number called 'the function' and a number called 'the least arity'.
    a number called 'this arity' is element 'the function' of gen_function_arity.
    If 'this arity' is less than 'the least arity' then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a boolean called 'all numbers' is 'gen function is all numbers of' of 'the function' and 'this arity'.
    Return a boolean, 'all numbers'.

To 'gen function is all numbers of' with a number called 'the function' and a number called 'the arity'.
    a number called 'this arity' is element 'the function' of gen_function_arity.
    If 'this arity' is not 'the arity' then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the first parameter' is element 'the function' of gen_function_first_param.
    a number called 'the step' is 0.
    a boolean called 'all numbers' is true.
    While 'the step' is less than 'this arity',
        a number called 'the parameter' is 'the first parameter' add 'the step',
        a number called 'the kind' is element 'the parameter' of gen_param_kind,
        If 'the kind' is not 0 then,
            Set 'all numbers' to false.
        Set 'the step' to 'the step' add 1.
    Return a boolean, 'all numbers'.

(A function taking exactly one text: the sink a format string can be
 passed to, which is what 'gen leaf format sink' wants for its
 function-argument case.)

To 'gen manifest pick a text function'.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'how many functions' is gen_function_names's length.
    a number called 'the function' is 1.
    While 'the function' is less than or equal to 'how many functions',
        a number called 'this arity' is element 'the function' of gen_function_arity,
        a number called 'the first parameter' is element 'the function' of gen_function_first_param,
        a number called 'the kind' is 0,
        If 'this arity' is 1 then,
            Set 'the kind' to element 'the first parameter' of gen_param_kind.
        If 'this arity' is 1 and 'the kind' is 1 then,
            append 'the function' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the function' to 'the function' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_function to element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    Return a boolean, true.

(A flag of a given type, for the argv builder and its assertions. The
 scratch flag is excluded: the harness supplies its value, so passing it
 a second value would fight with the plumbing that gives a program its
 own directory.)

To 'gen manifest pick a flag of kind' with a number called 'the kind'.
    a list called 'the candidates' is [].
    a number called 'how many flags' is gen_flag_names's length.
    a number called 'the flag' is 1.
    While 'the flag' is less than or equal to 'how many flags',
        a number called 'this kind' is element 'the flag' of gen_flag_kind,
        a number called 'the role' is element 'the flag' of gen_flag_role,
        If 'this kind' is 'the kind' and 'the role' is 0 then,
            append 'the flag' to 'the candidates'.
        Set 'the flag' to 'the flag' add 1.
    a number called 'how many candidates' is 'the candidates's length.
    If 'how many candidates' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many candidates'.
    a number called 'the slot' is 'the draw' add 1.
    Set gen_pick_flag to element 'the slot' of 'the candidates'.
    Return a boolean, true.

(Any flag at all, scratch included - 'gen leaf flag read' only reads
 them, and reading the scratch flag is as good a read as any.)

To 'gen manifest pick any flag'.
    a number called 'how many flags' is gen_flag_names's length.
    If 'how many flags' is 0 then,
        Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the draw' is 'rng below' of 'how many flags'.
    Set gen_pick_flag to 'the draw' add 1.
    Return a boolean, true.

(The stand-aside. A leaf whose shape this program's prelude cannot host
 emits this instead: one Print of an ordinary expression, which is legal
 at every depth and closes a block cleanly, and which honours `nested`
 so it can sit anywhere the leaf it replaced could.

 One helper rather than each leaf naming its own substitute, because the
 substitute is not the interesting part - what matters is that a leaf
 never assumes the prelude has a shape, and that the program still gets
 a statement where one was asked for.)

To 'gen manifest stand aside' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the expression' is 'gen expr'.
    a text called line is "Print {'the expression'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [line].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.
    Return a boolean, false.
